Notes on what I did **not** implement exactly:

- **Challenging-stage "PERFECT!" (10,000) bonus** is awarded only for hitting all 40; the per-wave 1,000 bonus is granted approximately (a wave counts as cleared once its 8 have left the screen), not strictly requiring all 8 of that wave to be shot.
- **Tractor-beam edge cases**: shooting a *diving* Boss while it holds your ship frees and docks it (implemented); but I did not add a separate "escort-shot-to-free-the-captive" path — freeing is tied to destroying the diving Boss itself. Shooting the beam or killing an in-formation Boss destroys/loses the captive as specified.
- **Boss dive scoring** awards 400 + 400 per escort that was shot down together (400 / 800 / 1,600 scale) rather than a fixed 800/1,600 tier; single-Boss dives are always 400.
- **Stage flags** follow the arcade denominations but use one flag per unit for stages under 10 (so e.g. stage 9 shows nine small flags); grouping into "×N" is only shown at the 10/20/30/50 tiers.
- A couple of minor polish items are simplified: the attract screen uses a static demo scene instead of a live scripted enemy choreography, and there is no optional CRT scanline overlay (the crisp pixelated scale-up is used).
